==Battleground==
*4 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*2 [[Dark Otter]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Techn-Old Hyena]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**6 [[Dark Otter]]s spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**2 [[Dolphina]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage debuts Techn-Old Hyena, an enemy with a really bad name. Since Techn-Old has an extremely long warp time, either use [[Warp Immunity|Warp Immune]] meatshields, such as [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]], [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]], or even [[sports Day Cat (Rare Cat)|Rampage cats]], or weak meatshields. For the Dark enemies, [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] does very well, while for cleaning up the hyena itself [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], & [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] work fine.

